cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark dataset, please cite both the dataset itself (using the metadata below) and the accompanying paper (see 'preferred-citation')."
type: dataset
title: "SimilCode Benchmark: A Dual-Language Source-Code Similarity Dataset for the Evaluation of AI-Based Detectors"
abstract: >
  SimilCode Benchmark is a controlled dataset of 120 source-code pairs in C#
  and Java (15 reference programs per language, four similarity categories:
  identical, functional, structural and different) for evaluating source-code
  similarity detectors in programming education. It includes the raw results
  of a replicated evaluation of four commercial large language models
  (GPT-5.5, DeepSeek-V4-pro, Gemini 3.1 Pro and Claude Opus 5; 1,440
  evaluations, three replicas per pair and model) and the outputs of Moss,
  JPlag and Dolos on the same pairs; a classification of the pairs by code-clone
  type; a second run with 84 copies of the reference programs rewritten with
  generative AI (by a local open-weight model and by commercial models),
  verified by execution and scored together with independent solutions to the
  same exercises (1,368 LLM evaluations and the three detectors), including
  the refusals of the generators; the validation corpus and predictions of the
  Big O estimator of SimilCode; and scripts that reproduce the reported numbers
  without calling any API.
version: 2.3.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
license: CC-BY-4.0
